      "behaviour": "Bits 1 and 0 select the interlace mode, 3 being interlace and video; bit 2 row and column addressing; bit 4 display enable skew; bit 5 cursor skew. Bits 3, 6 and 7 serve the variants with transparent update, and MAME logs a nonzero value as unsupported on chips without it.",
